 "/athletes/111073"} "Viktor Knoch"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/137350"} "Csaba Burján"] " " [:a {:href "/countries/HUN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/HUN.png"}] "HUN"] " / 22 February 2018 / " [:a {:href "/records/event_name/546"} "Details"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "With all eight nations seeing themselves capable of winning a medal in the event, the semi-finals were already a tense affair. Home favorites China seemed to be eliminated in the first heat, after a fall of " [:a {:href "/athletes/148133"} "Li Wenlong"] ". Only after a lengthy referee review were they advanced to the final – a rare occurrence in short-track without another team being disqualified. Defending gold medalist Hungary were outpaced in the second heat, as Korea, ROC, and Netherlands battled it out for the top-two spots. Reigning World Champions Netherlands were leading with two laps to go, but were passed by Korea and, on the line by ROC, missing the final by a mere 0.002 seconds."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The five-team final saw Korea lead the way most of the first half of the race, but with all teams still in close contention. At 18 laps, Gwak made a slight misstep, leaving room for Canada to gain first place. Sitting behind Korea in third, China’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/148134"} "Sun Long"] " lost his balance fell, leaving the Chinese with no chance of a medal. The fall left a gap between Canada/Korea and ROC/Italy, which was never closed again. The Koreans made a few attempts to regain the lead, but Canada powered away in the end to win their fourth gold in the event. It was also the fourth Olympic gold for " [:a {:href "/athletes/109918"} "Charles Hamelin"] ", making him only the fourth short-track skater to achieve this, after " [:a {:href "/athletes/101557"} "Viktor An"] ", " [:a {:href "/athletes/109921"} "Wang Meng"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/80843"} "Jeon I-Gyeong"] "."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The decision for bronze only came at the finish line, with " [:a {:href "/athletes/148510"} "Pietro Sighel"] " taking the medal for Italy, stretching his leg 0.009 ahead of ROC."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Helmet Nr"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Position Last Race"] [:th {} "Positions"] [:th {} "Best Time"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} "Canada"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CAN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CAN.png"}] "CAN"]] [:td {} "AF-1"] [:td {} "1"] [:td {} "6:38.752"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "11"} [:a {:href "/athletes/109918"} "Charles Hamelin"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/148017"} "Maxime Laoun"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/148016"} "Steven Dubois"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/148018"} "Jordan Pierre-Gilles"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/136930"} "Pascal Dion"]]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} "Republic of Korea"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/KOR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/KOR.png"}] "KOR"]] [:td {} "AF-2"] [:td {} "1"] [:td {} "6:37.879"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "11"} [:a {:href "/athletes/148602"} "Lee Jun-Seo"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/148601"} "Kim Dong-Uk"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/137644"} "Hwang Dae-Heon"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/119776"} "Gwak Yun-Gi"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/148603"} "Park Jang-Hyeok"]]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} "Italy"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ITA"} [:img {:style "padding-ri